<title>UK: UK reserves fall underlying $99 mln in February.</title>
<headline>UK reserves fall underlying $99 mln in February.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's gold and currency reserves fell an underlying $99 million in February, the Treasury said. (IN MLN DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED)</p>
<p>					 February	     January</p>
<p>  Underlying reserves		-99		  + one</p>
<p> Actual reserves		  - 114	    - 2,733</p>
<p> Total actual reserves     43.45 billion	 43.57 billion</p>
<p>The underlying change excludes factors included in the total change (IN MLN OF DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED</p>
<p>ECU Treasury Bills issued</p>
<p> exceeded those maturing	 + one		    + three</p>
<p>ECU Treasury Notes maturing</p>
<p> exceeded those issued	   -------		  - 2,496</p>
<p>Repayments under the</p>
<p> exchange cover scheme (ECS)   - 16			 - 146</p>
<p>Revaluation payment from EMI</p>
<p> swap				  -------		     + 12</p>
<p>Debt payments assigned from</p>
<p> public sector		     -------		    - 105</p>
<p> Total of adjustments		15			 2,732</p>
<p> Underlying change		 - 99			 + one</p>
